comments.body:
Here's an alternative that I like better: https://github.com/ajtowns/bitcoin/commits/202611-pr36521-ser/

It modifes ParamsStream to also support mutable state if the params have a State class and an InitState method, and provides a `GetState` function to access/modify that state. At the caller side, you just have:

```c++
static constexpr TransactionSerParams TX_WITH_WITNESS_BLOCK_LIMIT{
    .allow_witness = true, .reject_empty = true, .max_weight = MAX_BLOCK_TXS_WEIGHT
};

vRecv >> TX_WITH_WITNESS_BLOCK_LIMIT(*pblock);
```

