> [c655a69](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36521/changes/c655a696d8d1013bf61b815ba7b477840d31765c) _p2p: limit the weight of transactions and blocks while deserializing_:

We can reuse the `CTxIn` and `CTxOut` serializers here and write transactions directly into the block buffer.

As a follow-up (or prerequisite), we should extract and generalize the block creator in this benchmark along the lines of [#32554](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/32554), so a shared generator can replace the hardcoded raw block fixture.

